abstract: >-
  Benchmarks for evaluating generated DNA against matched natural sequence.
  Covers per-window composition and divergence, calibration of that divergence
  against natural window-to-window variation, shallow and deep detectability,
  drift from the conditioning prompt, k-mer spectra, chaos game representation,
  nullomers, transcription factor binding sites and non-B DNA structure, plus
  reusable interventions for constraining generation at training and sampling
  time.
keywords:
  - genomics
  - genomic language models
  - benchmark
  - synthetic DNA
  - sequence generation
  - non-B DNA
  - nullomers
  - k-mer spectra
